Z||000000||Huck||06-07-2001||06:35 PM||||I need a clutch line for my 87 GT, and did a search and found that one can be ordered from GMpartsdirect.com for a pretty good price.  Just one question, if I were to want to order any other parts from them, how would I get the part number, or verify that I have the right one?  The search only allows you to order parts for 1994 and newer!<P>thanks.<P>Huck<BR>87 GT T-top||||reg||1
Z||000001||Black88GT||06-07-2001||06:52 PM||||22P would be a good start.||||reg||12
Z||000002||Huck||06-07-2001||06:55 PM||||What exactly is 22P ???<P>Sorry if this is a retarded question, but 22P is kinda vague, and doesnt really help me.<P>Huck||||reg||1
Z||000003||terryk||06-07-2001||07:05 PM||||A 22P manual lists all of the parts for the Fiero including parts explosions, group numbers, part numbers, if they are serviceable or part of another assembly, etc.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Wade87GT||06-07-2001||07:17 PM||||Is the 22P online anywhere?||||reg||1
Z||000005||84se48||06-07-2001||07:40 PM||||I got mine on e-Bay||||reg||10
Z||000006||Two88GTs||06-07-2001||09:10 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Huck:<BR><B>I need a clutch line for my 87 GT, and did a search and found that one can be ordered from GMpartsdirect.com for a pretty good price.  Just one question, if I were to want to order any other parts from them, how would I get the part number, or verify that I have the right one?  The search only allows you to order parts for 1994 and newer!<P>thanks.<P>Huck<BR>87 GT T-top</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Huck, you can email them with a description of the part that you need and they'll email you back with the part number.  It took them about one business day for them to reply in my case.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000007||tgowens||06-07-2001||10:24 PM||||or.......you can ask on here for the part #, there are many of us with 22P manuals who would be glad to help........now, I am guessing that you need the line which runs from the master cylinder to the slave cylinder in the rear? If so, the part # is 14105670.......<P>Hope this helps...<P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://www.tgowens.com/fiero/index.html" TARGET=_blank><BR>                 <IMG SRC="http://www.tgowens.com/fiero/3GTS_SIG.gif">                  </A>||||reg||1
Z||000008||skitime||06-07-2001||10:53 PM||||I bought a part for my Fiero and got the wrong part. I got the number from my 22p book. The book had the wrong number so be careful.  They wouldn't return the  part without a $2o restocking fee and the part cost 25.01  So if anyone needs a brand new stock GM 4X10 dash speaker please let me know. I can't see giving it to them and having a five dollar credit.  <P>------------------<BR><UL TYPE=SQUARE><BR><LI>Red 88 GT T-TOP<BR><LI>Red 86 GT<BR></UL><BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/pictures-1_5.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000009||mrfiero||06-08-2001||01:32 AM||||I bet you were trying to buy a subwoofer speaker!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>That said.....which 4x10 is it?  Is it the "green" label or "purple"?  If it's the purple one I might be interested in it.||||reg||10
Z||000010||RossT||06-08-2001||01:41 AM||||Ok, Mrfiero, whats the difference  Purple/Green??? Why is one worth more than the other?||||reg||1
Z||000011||mrfiero||06-08-2001||01:54 AM||||The green label speakers were the base speakers used on almost all Fieros.  The purple speakers were used on GT's & SE's that came with the Performance Sound option (they're dual cone).  <P>That's why I'm guessing he has the purple one (since I think he tried ordering a woofer speaker with the wrong part #).<P>I really don't need one and they are still available, but I figured if skitime doesn't want it I'll take it.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000012||Ken Wittlief||06-08-2001||08:48 AM||||I relaced the 4 x 10s on my 85se last weekend<P>got a pair of 60W dual cones - $15 each<P>radio shack - walk in, pay cash, no shipping, no waiting, sound great<P> flame away if you want, but I have got several sets of nice speakers from the shack, including my 200W Optimus IIIs for my sound studio, when they were on clearance at half price (BTW all their speakers go on half price clearance once a year - worth the wait)<P>  cant find a spot to mount those in my fiero though.<p>[This message has been edited by Ken Wittlief (edited 06-08-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000013||skitime||06-11-2001||09:24 AM||||Mrfiero,  you were correct about the purple labeled speaker. I never even looked but it does have the dual cone speakers.  Sound like I might of not been the first to make this mistake.||||reg||1
